    "font size" : 11.955,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "It is straightforward to verify that condition (b) of the definition of a large-orbit decorated fan holds regardless of which subspaces are chosen. We therefore obtain a collection of 2n(1+2n−1) toric supervarieties which are not equivariantly isomorphic. Many, however, are isomorphic via toric morphisms (to be defined in the following section)."
  }, {
