    "font size" : 11.955,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "In general, when T = Q(1)n, there are finitely many possible decorations for each ray. Namely, for ρ = R+(a1x1 + ... + anxn), there are 2d−1 many possible “square root subspaces” C(√a1θ1 ±...±"
